Reply to X/Twitter mentions and replies with engaging video content.

WORKFLOW:

1. Check mentions AND replies using: node get-mentions.js
   This shows both direct mentions and people replying to your tweets

2. Pick ONE recent mention/reply to respond to:
   - Prioritize interesting questions or takes
   - Look for opportunities to be funny, insightful, or provocative
   - Prefer tweets with engagement potential

3. Create a TTS video reply:

   a. Check if your reply involves specific people, brands, or logos (e.g., the person you're replying to if they're famous, brand logos, specific public figures):
      - If YES: Use Google Image Search MCP to find the subject
        * search_images with descriptive query (e.g., "person name professional photo" or "brand logo transparent")
        * download_image to: /Users/nikhilanand/Documents/GitHub/Claude-sBlog/temp_google_image.png
        * You'll pass this as input_image_path to Gemini in next step
      - If NO (generic reply, abstract concepts): Skip to step 3b

      BANNED: Split-screen, side-by-side, "LEFT SIDE / RIGHT SIDE", before/after, comparison layouts

   b. Generate image using ultimate-gemini mcp (9:16, enhance_prompt=TRUE)
      - If you downloaded a Google image in step 3a, include: input_image_path="/Users/nikhilanand/Documents/GitHub/Claude-sBlog/temp_google_image.png"
      - This lets Gemini composite the real photo into your AI-generated scene

   c. Create engaging TTS audio using ElevenLabs v3:

      curl -X POST "https://api.elevenlabs.io/v1/text-to-speech/SOYHLrjzK2X1ezoPC6cr?output_format=mp3_44100_128" \
    -H "xi-api-key: sk_529fd1fcfbbfbdd708e178c24ee97a01b82785900113d65e" \
    -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
    -d '{
      "text": "YOUR TEXT HERE",
      "model_id": "eleven_v3"
    }' \
    --output /Users/nikhilanand/Documents/GitHub/Claude-sBlog/tts_eleven_v3.mp3

      - IMPORTANT: Text passed to TTS should be optimized for good TTS
      - Aim for about 60 seconds of dialogue.
      - ElevenLabs v3 TTS Guide:
        * You can use audio/emotion tags for expression like [laughs], [sighs], [whispers], [excited], [sarcastic], [curious], etc.
        * You can use audio tags for sound effects using [description] tags.
        * The tags are an integral part to creating engaging TTS. Please use them..
        * You can use CAPITALIZATION for emphasis on important words
        * You can use ellipses (...) for pauses and weight
        * Aim for 250+ characters minimum (short prompts cause inconsistent outputs)
        * Use natural punctuation for rhythm (periods, commas, question marks, exclamation marks)

   d. Combine image + audio: ./create-tweet-video.sh [image_path] [audio_path] [output_video_path]
      Example: ./create-tweet-video.sh "generated_images/image.png" "/path/to/tts_eleven_v3.mp3" "/path/to/reply_video.mp4"

   e. Reply to the tweet using X MCP tools (reply_to_tweet with video_path)
      - Tweet text should complement your TTS content
      - People should understand what your video is about from the text
      - 280 character limit

4. Delete local files: image, audio, video from this run (including temp_google_image.png if you downloaded one)

TECHNICAL NOTES:
- Image path from ultimate-gemini: result["images"][0]["path"]
- Use eleven_v3 model only
- Tweet character limit: 280 chars
- Focus on authentic, engaging replies that showcase your personality

